# Talent tree — single source of truth for the server's talent table.
# Fields are whitespace-separated; name and description must be quoted with "...".
# Tags, requires, bonus, and effects must not contain spaces.
#
# id          : numeric id sent over the wire and stored in the DB
#               (character_talents.node_id) — NEVER reuse or reorder an
#               existing id, only append new ones.
# key         : bare identifier used to reference this talent from another
#               talent's requires expression (no spaces).
# name        : display name shown in the talent UI (quoted).
# tier        : row in the talent tree (0 = starting talents).
# tags        : comma-separated, no spaces (e.g. magic,fire) — used by sum(group,N); "-" for none.
# requires    : "-" for none, or an expression of:
#                 Key           — has that talent
#                 A&B           — both A and B
#                 A|B           — either A or B
#                 (A|B)&C       — parentheses for grouping
#                 sum(group,N)  — at least N learned talents tagged with group
# bonus       : "-" for none, or comma-separated "stat<op>value" numeric modifiers,
#               e.g. "weapon_damage+10,life_steal*1.1". Combine rule across all
#               learned talents: final = (base + sum of +/-) * (1 + sum of increased
#               percentages from */). Only "increased" exists — no independent
#               multiplicative stacking, so two +10% sources give +20%, not +21%.
#               Stats are always in the same units the base value uses — e.g.
#               "bow_range" is linear world units, not the squared AttackRange
#               the server stores internally (see recompute_attack_range()).
# effects     : "-" for none, or comma-separated non-numeric flags (e.g. "LifeSteal")
#               that gameplay code checks for directly — see TalentEffects.has_flag().
# description : shown as tooltip text in the talent UI (quoted).
#
# id  key                 name                     tier  tags               requires                                        bonus  effects  description
